.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Own layers, an isolated physics world, a camera, timers and simulation time\&. 

Create gameplay first and HUD second: scenes draw in construction order above legacy layers\&. Both can target the same \fBPort\fP\&. Pausing gameplay keeps drawing its held pose while the HUD continues to animate and receive its own timer events\&. Raw input is controlled separately with \fBsetInputEnabled(boolean)\fP\&.

.PP
addLayer(layer) adopts a detached layer or a layer from the legacy factory\&. removeLayer(layer) detaches without destroying sprites or their physical state; the caller must attach it elsewhere or clean it up\&. disposeLayer(layer) destroys an attached layer\&. \fBdispose()\fP is idempotent, cancels timers and subscriptions, and destroys remaining attached layers\&. Detached layers survive\&. Cross-layer physics constraints must be disconnected before detachment\&. Mutation of layer membership must occur outside scene traversal\&. Deferred disposal is safe inside callbacks\&.

.PP
The effective layer camera is its explicit override, otherwise its \fBScene\fP camera, otherwise its \fBPort\fP camera\&. \fBScene\fP cameras and layer overrides advance once on the owning scene clock\&. A camera cannot be automatically advanced by two scenes\&.

.PP
advance(seconds), setFixedStep(seconds), \fBgetSimulationTime()\fP and \fBgetDroppedTime()\fP use seconds\&. setManual(true) disables automatic host advancement\&. Fixed step 0 selects variable stepping; a positive value selects fixed stepping\&. Updates admit at most 0\&.25 seconds of host time and run at most eight fixed steps\&. Excess whole steps are discarded and reported by \fBgetDroppedTime()\fP; discarded time does not fire logical timers\&. setTimeScale(scale) accepts finite nonnegative values\&. Zero freezes advancement without setting \fBisPaused()\fP\&. Resume adds no paused-time debt\&.

.PP
setInterpolation(true) enables read-only interpolation of sprite root translation, scale and shortest-path rotation during fixed-step rendering\&. Mounted sprites inherit the parent correction\&. Queries and physics retain authoritative state; skeletal poses and camera poses use current state\&. A teleport resets presentation\&.

.PP
\fBScene\fP timer delays and intervals use milliseconds\&. IDs are positive and local to each scene\&. onTimeout(callback, delayMs) and onInterval(callback, intervalMs) return cancellable handles\&. Callbacks receive the timer event synchronously\&. Repeating intervals must be positive; zero-delay one-shots wait for the next update\&. Timers fire before animation at an update boundary, at most once per step, and newly created timers wait for a later boundary\&. \fBScene\fP pause includes timers created while paused\&. \fBScene\fP resume preserves individually paused timers\&. Scaling affects logical deadlines; getWhenTimerFiresNext(id) returns the logical deadline in milliseconds, or -1 for an absent or paused timer\&.

.PP
subscribe(emitter, eventType, callback) returns a cancellable external registration and disconnects it on explicit \fBdispose()\fP\&. Pause does not suppress raw external events\&. Async work and sound servicing continue independently; applications decide when to apply late results and pause gameplay voices\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Rendering requires a graphics-capable build\&. Manual simulation, timers and camera animation are available headlessly\&. Explicitly dispose scenes when leaving a level; garbage collection is not a lifecycle boundary\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const gameplay = new pdg\&.Scene();
gameplay\&.setFixedStep(1 / 60);
gameplay\&.setInterpolation(true);
const hud = new pdg\&.Scene();
const worldLayer = gameplay\&.createSpriteLayer();
const hudLayer = hud\&.createSpriteLayer();
worldLayer\&.setSpritePort(port);
hudLayer\&.setSpritePort(port);
hud\&.onInterval(function () { caret\&.setOpacity(caret\&.getOpacity() ? 0 : 1); }, 500);
gameplay\&.pause();     // HUD continues above the held gameplay image\&.
gameplay\&.resume();
// On leaving this level:
gameplay\&.dispose();
hud\&.dispose();
.fi
.PP
 
