.SS "\fBCollisionQueryHit\fP raycast (\fBPoint\fP start, \fBPoint\fP end, \fBCollisionQueryOptions\fP options = \fRundefined\fP)"

.PP
Return the closest accepted segment entry hit, or null\&. Queries inspect current authoritative scene geometry before stepping and while paused, independently of cameras, render interpolation, visibility, input and collision-response switches\&. Enabled attached \fBSprite\fP, \fBPart\fP and \fBParticle\fP colliders are eligible, including bodyless colliders\&. Basic and Chipmunk configurations use the same geometry algorithms\&. Touching counts and a zero-length ray tests containment\&. Call outside scene update/draw traversal\&. Queries during \fBadvance()\fP, including timer and contact callbacks, and recursive queries from predicates throw\&. Predicates must not mutate geometry, scene membership or results, advance scenes, or dispose scenes or layers\&. Predicate errors propagate and leave the reused array empty\&.

.PP
The scene reuses one array and a pool of hit records, including their \fBPoint\fP and \fBVector\fP fields\&. All returned arrays and hits are valid until the next query on that scene or disposal\&. This includes single-hit queries\&. Copy fields and coordinates when keeping a result; copying the array alone does not copy its hit records\&. Queries on another scene do not invalidate these results\&. Treat returned arrays, records and coordinates as read-only\&. Disposal empties the array and clears its collider references\&. Hit records retain colliders while active; shape IDs may cease to exist after geometry changes\&.

.PP
 
.PP
\fBShared query options\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Field  Default  Meaning  maxHits  16  Overlap limit, integer 0 to 1048576; zero returns an empty array\&. Cast array overloads take maxHits as a separate parameter\&.  layerMask  4294967295  Unsigned 32-bit mask intersecting layer queryBits\&. Zero selects none\&. Layers default to bit 1\&.  layers  All scene layers  Optional \fBSpriteLayer\fP array intersected with layerMask\&. Empty selects none; foreign/detached layers throw\&.  categoryMask  4294967295  Unsigned 32-bit mask intersecting collider categories\&.  includeSensors  true  Include sensor colliders\&.  excludedColliders  Empty  \fBCollider\fP identities to exclude\&.  excludedBodies  Empty  \fBPhysicsBody\fP identities whose colliders are excluded\&.  predicate  None  Synchronous boolean function(collider), called once per eligible collider before limiting results\&.  

.PP
\fBCollisionQueryHit fields\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Field  Meaning  collider, shapeId  \fBCollider\fP and public shape identity\&.  point  Cast target point or nearest point on filled geometry\&. Initial overlaps can return an interior point\&.  normal  Outward normal toward the query; zero for initial overlaps and nearest points inside a shape\&.  fraction  Cast travel fraction in [0,1]\&.  distance  Cast travel distance or nearest filled-geometry distance in world units\&.  initialOverlap  Cast starts touching/overlapping; distance and fraction are zero\&.  

.PP
Overlap results expose identity only; other fields are zero\&. Array overloads of raycast(start, end, maxHits, options) and sweepCircle(center, radius, delta, maxHits, options), and overlap methods, return at most maxHits entries, sorted by distance, collider ID and shape ID\&. Overlaps use identity ordering\&. Decomposition pieces do not duplicate a public shape hit\&. Arrays have exactly the stored hit count; a miss returns an empty array\&. No truncation flag is exposed\&. Circle sweeps translate against current stationary geometry; nonuniform scale/shear uses the existing curved-boundary approximation\&. Layer queryBits are runtime settings and are not serialized in layer snapshots\&. Finite coordinates and nonnegative finite radii/distances are required\&. Boxes must have positive dimensions\&. Invalid requests throw\&. 

.PP
Storage is reused after warming up to the requested capacity\&. Geometry snapshots, candidate collection, script/native argument transport and sorting may still allocate; the API does not promise allocation-free queries\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstart\fP \fBScene\fP world-space segment start\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP \fBScene\fP world-space segment end\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP Optional selection; see \fBscene_collision_query_options\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Closest accepted \fBCollisionQueryHit\fP, or null\&. The hit is reused on the next query\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Attach searched layers to a live scene; no physics step is required\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const game = new pdg\&.Scene();
const terrain = game\&.createSpriteLayer();
terrain\&.createSprite()\&.setupCollider()\&.setBox(new pdg\&.Rect(100, 0, 120, 100));
const hit = game\&.raycast(new pdg\&.Point(0, 50), new pdg\&.Point(200, 50));
if (hit) console\&.log(hit\&.distance); // 100 world units
const hits = game\&.overlapCircle(new pdg\&.Point(110, 50), 20, {maxHits: 8});
for (const entry of hits) console\&.log(entry\&.shapeId);
// Keep a copy before another query reuses entry and its coordinate objects\&.
const saved = hits\&.map(entry => ({collider: entry\&.collider, shapeId: entry\&.shapeId}));
game\&.dispose();

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP

